# 高频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List03核心词汇

impact /ˈɪmpækt/ n./v. 影响；冲击 Technology has had a profound impact on education. 科技对教育产生了深远的影响。
indicate /ˈɪndɪkeɪt/ v. 表明；指示 Research indicates that exercise improves mental health. 研究表明运动能改善心理健康。
interpret /ɪnˈtɜːprɪt/ v. 解释；翻译 Different people may interpret this data differently. 不同的人可能对这些数据有不同的解读。
investigate /ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/ v. 调查 The police are investigating the incident. 警方正在调查这起事件。
maintain /meɪnˈteɪn/ v. 维持；保养 We must maintain high standards of quality. 我们必须保持高质量标准。
mechanism /ˈmekənɪzəm/ n. 机制；方法 The market has its own self-correcting mechanism. 市场有其自我调节机制。
obtain /əbˈteɪn/ v. 获得 She obtained a degree in law from Peking University. 她获得了北京大学的法学学位。
obvious /ˈɒbviəs/ adj. 明显的 It is obvious that the plan needs revision. 很明显这个计划需要修改。
occupy /ˈɒkjupaɪ/ v. 占据；从事 Reading occupies most of her free time. 阅读占据了她大部分的空闲时间。
participate /pɑːˈtɪsɪpeɪt/ v. 参加 All students are encouraged to participate in the discussion. 鼓励所有学生参与讨论。
perceive /pəˈsiːv/ v. 感知；认为 The public perceives this as a serious problem. 公众认为这是一个严重的问题。
phenomenon /fəˈnɒmɪnən/ n. 现象 Global warming is a well-documented phenomenon. 全球变暖是一个有充分记录的现象。
potential /pəˈtenʃəl/ adj./n. 潜在的；潜力 Every child has the potential to succeed. 每个孩子都有成功的潜力。
previous /ˈpriːviəs/ adj. 先前的 Previous studies have shown similar results. 之前的研究显示了类似的结果。
primary /ˈpraɪməri/ adj. 主要的；初级的 Education is the primary focus of this policy. 教育是这项政策的主要焦点。
principle /ˈprɪnsəpl/ n. 原则；原理 The principle of equality is fundamental to democracy. 平等原则是民主的基础。
prior /ˈpraɪə(r)/ adj./adv. 在前的；优先的 Prior to the meeting, please review the documents. 会议前请审阅文件。
promote /prəˈməʊt/ v. 促进；推广 The government aims to promote economic growth. 政府旨在促进经济增长。
proportion /prəˈpɔːʃn/ n. 比例 A large proportion of the budget is spent on defense. 预算的很大一部分用于国防。
pursue /pəˈsjuː/ v. 追求；从事 She decided to pursue a career in medicine. 她决定从事医学事业。
range /reɪndʒ/ n./v. 范围；变化 The store offers a wide range of products. 这家商店提供各种各样的产品。
region /ˈriːdʒən/ n. 地区 This region is known for its natural beauty. 这个地区以其自然美景而闻名。
regulate /ˈreɡjuleɪt/ v. 管理；调节 The government should regulate financial markets. 政府应该监管金融市场。
relate /rɪˈleɪt/ v. 联系；叙述 How does this relate to our original question? 这与我们最初的问题有什么关系？
rely /rɪˈlaɪ/ v. 依赖 We cannot rely solely on technology to solve this problem. 我们不能仅仅依赖技术来解决这个问题。
remove /rɪˈmuːv/ v. 移除；消除 We need to remove all obstacles to progress. 我们需要消除所有进步的障碍。
resource /rɪˈsɔːs/ n. 资源 Natural resources are limited. 自然资源是有限的。
restrict /rɪˈstrɪkt/ v. 限制 The new law restricts smoking in public places. 新法律限制在公共场所吸烟。
secure /sɪˈkjʊə(r)/ adj./v. 安全的；获得 We must secure funding for the project. 我们必须为项目获得资金。
seek /siːk/ v. 寻求 Many young people seek opportunities abroad. 许多年轻人到国外寻求机会。
